 ## Unreleased
 
+- Register the independent stable APT/RPM public certificates and reviewed
+  signing roles, while retaining the disabled stable channel and preview
+  publication inputs.
+
 - Accept encrypted current-subkey and passphrase files for local family signing,
   retaining the existing CI environment inputs and verification, with native
   TEST ONLY signing regression coverage. Document Mac local stable-key custody;
diff --git a/docs/release-contract.md b/docs/release-contract.md
index 3831a44..ceb015e 100644
--- a/docs/release-contract.md
+++ b/docs/release-contract.md
@@ -370,6 +370,15 @@ Promoting an RPM preserves the same unsigned payload, NEVRA, and provenance,
 but its bytes change when it is signed with the independent stable key. This
 custody choice does not enable the stable channel or authorize publication.
 
+The optional `manifests/stable-public-keys.json` declaration registers only the
+two independent stable public certificates and their exact signing roles. It
+reuses public-certificate validation and the existing lifetime policy, with
+fingerprint and short-key-ID uniqueness across preview and stable. The complete
+declaration and both certificates must be present together. Older controls
+without any stable registration remain valid. Registration changes neither the
+disabled stable channel nor the preview manifest, snapshot, archive or bootstrap
+certificate inputs; it creates no GitHub secret or signing Environment.
+
 The credential-free TEST ONLY PR drill also exercises the local file and
 existing environment inputs with tiny data-only packages and independent
 ephemeral APT/RPM keys, plus the stdin subkey option. After signing, it removes
diff --git a/keys/README.md b/keys/README.md
index 399105b..7ccd185 100644
--- a/keys/README.md
+++ b/keys/README.md
@@ -48,6 +48,19 @@ on the Mac or NAS, and never enter GitHub-hosted CI; see the
 [release contract](../docs/release-contract.md). This is an online-workstation
 model, not an offline-signing claim.
 
+`manifests/stable-public-keys.json` is the sole public role declaration for
+`apt-stable.asc` and `rpm-stable.asc`. It records only the certificate path and
+primary/current/next/historical fingerprints; it has no secret, Environment or
+publication-enable fields. The same public certificate checks and 30/45/180-day
+policy apply, and full fingerprints plus 16-hex and 8-hex key IDs must be unique
+across both channels and both package families. Historical control roots may
+omit this entire registration; a partial registration is rejected.
+
+This registration does not enable stable signing or publication. Preview
+snapshots, audit archives and bootstrap packages continue to contain only
+their reviewed preview certificates. Stable private material remains on the
+operator's Mac; the public role declaration is not backup-recovery evidence.
+
 For local signing, `scripts/sign-package-family.py` accepts exactly one of
 `--secret-subkey-base64-file`, `--secret-subkey-base64-stdin`, or the existing
 `--secret-subkey-base64-env`, and exactly one of `--passphrase-file` or
